{
    "background_story": "Killer was a proud and powerful stallion from the rolling hills of Vermont. Born and raised on a farm just outside of Montpelier, he was named for his feisty spirit and untamed mane. Despite his rugged exterior, Killer had a gentle soul and a strong work ethic. He spent his days plowing the fields and carrying riders through the picturesque countryside. In the winter, Killer would proudly pull a horse-drawn sleigh through the snow-covered streets of Montpelier, his breath misting in the cold air. As the capital city's unofficial mascot, Killer became a beloved fixture, symbolizing the strength and beauty of the Green Mountain State. His legend grew, and he was often called upon to lead parades and festivals, his spirit and strength inspiring all who saw him.",
